 "lines": [
  {
   "text": "In 1970, Oregon tried to get rid of a dead whale with half a ton of dynamite.",
   "s": 0.12,
   "e": 5.123
  },
  {
   "text": "A forty-five-foot sperm whale had washed up on the beach in Florence, and it stank.",
   "s": 5.423,
   "e": 9.969
  },
  {
   "text": "So the highway department made a plan: blow it into tiny pieces for the seagulls.",
   "s": 10.269,
   "e": 14.795
  },
  {
   "text": "They packed twenty cases of dynamite around it.",
   "s": 15.095,
   "e": 17.463
  },
  {
   "text": "A crowd gathered to watch.",
   "s": 17.764,
   "e": 19.219
  },
  {
   "text": "Boom!",
   "s": 19.519,
   "e": 19.997
  },
  {
   "text": "Then it started raining whale.",
   "s": 20.297,
   "e": 21.682
  },
  {
   "text": "Blubber flew everywhere, and one chunk crushed a brand-new car a quarter mile away.",
   "s": 21.982,
   "e": 26.415
  },
  {
   "text": "And most of the whale was still on the beach.",
   "s": 26.715,
   "e": 28.711
  }
 ],
